# Max's visit (Alex, 2026-11-13; every line here is a DRAFT for Alex). The format is described at
# the top of scripts/story.gd.
# After about four hours of play (data/economy.json "story" max_visit_hours; main.gd
# _update_max_visit) Max drives out to the farm to win Nora back. She chooses whether to give
# him a chance. Either way he shows his true colours before he's gone: say yes and he's soon
# selling Gran's farm and joking about her sweater; say no and the temper comes out. She sends him
# away. Flags: max_accepted or max_refused, then max_visit_done. He is a visitor
# (main.gd visitor()) in his own model, only here for this scene. Max is the ex who was called
# Daniel in earlier drafts (Alex, 2026-11-13).

== max_visit
@trigger event max_visit
@requires act1_done
@once
@fade out 0.8
@place nora 9.8 3.0 90
@place max 18.0 4.3 270
@camera 12.4 3.2 9
@fade in 1.0
> A car she knows pulls up at the end of the lane. Grey, clean, completely wrong out here.
Nora (surprised): No. No, no, no.
@walk max 11.3 2.6
@face max nora
@face nora max
@camera between max nora 6
Max (warm): Hey, Nor.
Nora (worried): Max. What are you doing here?
Max (warm): Your mum gave me the address. Don't be angry with her. I asked nicely.
Max (sad): You didn't answer my letter. Or the calls. So I drove. Six hours.
Max (wry): Look at you. Sheep. Actual sheep.
Nora (neutral): It's Gran's farm. I'm looking after it while she's in Florida.
Max (sad): I've been doing a lot of thinking. I've been seeing someone. A therapist, I mean. Not... someone.
Max (warm): I know I wasn't easy to live with. I know about the sweater. I'm sorry about the sweater.
Max (warm): Come home, Nora. Not today, I'm not stupid. But soon. Let me show you I've changed.
? He looks like the man she married. Almost.
- ...Okay. One chance. Show me. -> accept | set max_accepted
- No. I'm not coming back, Max. -> refuse | set max_refused
@label accept
Nora (sad): One chance. I mean it. One.
Max (happy): That's all I need. That's all I ever needed.
> He pulls her into a hug. Over her shoulder, he's already looking at the house.
Max (neutral): We'll get this place on the market. Your gran's not coming back from Florida, let's be honest.
Nora (surprised): It isn't mine to sell.
Max (wry): Then talk her round. You're good at that. And Nor? Lose the jumper. You look like a tea cosy.
> And there it is. The little laugh after, so it's a joke if she minds.
Nora (angry): No. Get in your car, Max.
Max (surprised): Nora, come on. I was joking.
Nora (angry): You're always joking. Go home. I am home.
@journal note Max came | I said yes. For about a minute. Then he was selling Gran's farm and laughing at my sweater, and I saw him the way I should have years ago. I sent him home.
@goto leaves
@label refuse
Max (sad): You don't mean that. You're upset. It's all the fresh air.
Nora (neutral): I mean it. I'm staying.
Max (angry): Six hours, Nora. I drove six hours for this.
> And there it is. The edge she spent years learning to step around.
Nora (neutral): Then you'd better start back before it's dark.
@journal note Max came | He drove six hours to tell me he'd changed, and it took him about two minutes to show me he hadn't. I told him no. My hands didn't even shake.
@label leaves
@walk max 18.0 4.3 nowait
> He walks back down the lane to the grey car. He doesn't look back. He never did.
@wait 2.0
Nora (sad): ...Okay.
@set max_visit_done
@camera player

# Rebecca, the police officer (Alex, 2026-11-15; every line is a DRAFT for Alex): once Max has come
# and been sent away, Nora can report him to her. Rebecca raises it the first time they talk after
# his visit (rebecca_max). Nora can report him there and then, or leave it: the offer stays open as
# "Report Max" on Rebecca's menu (rebecca_report), and if she hasn't reported him "max_return_days"
# days after his visit (data/economy.json "story"; main.gd max_return_due) he comes back once
# (max_return). Reported (the flag max_reported), Rebecca is waiting the next time he turns up at
# the lane (max_arrest; main.gd _update_max_visit plays it as soon as she is free). After that the
# flag max_arrested is set and he never comes again. It is an option: the game goes on if she
# never reports him.

== rebecca_max
@trigger talk rebecca
@requires max_visit_done
@requires !max_reported
@once
@face rebecca nora
@face nora rebecca
@camera between rebecca nora 6
Rebecca (neutral): Nora. Have you got a minute?
Rebecca (worried): Barbara saw a grey car out at Birchfield. A man who took his time leaving.
Nora (neutral): My ex. Max. He drove six hours to tell me he'd changed.
Rebecca (neutral): Had he?
Nora (sad): No.
Rebecca (warm): You don't owe me the rest of it. But a man who's been told to go and comes back is my job, not yours.
? She waits. There's no hurry in it.
- I want to report him. -> report | set max_reported
- Not today. -> later | set max_report_open
@label report
Nora (neutral): He knows where I live now. I don't want to spend my evenings watching the lane.
Rebecca (neutral): Then you won't. Leave it with me.
@goto done
@label later
Rebecca (warm): That's all right. The offer doesn't run out. Any day, any hour.
@label done
@camera player

== rebecca_report
@trigger event report_max
@requires max_report_open
@requires !max_reported
@face rebecca nora
@face nora rebecca
@camera between rebecca nora 6
Nora (neutral): Rebecca. About Max. I'd like to report him.
Rebecca (neutral): Good. Leave it with me.
@set max_reported
@camera player

== max_return
@trigger event max_return
@requires max_visit_done
@requires !max_reported
@once
@fade out 0.8
@place nora 9.8 3.0 90
@place max 18.0 4.3 270
@camera 12.4 3.2 9
@fade in 1.0
> The grey car is at the end of the lane again.
@walk max 11.6 2.7
@face max nora
@face nora max
@camera between max nora 6
Max (warm): I was passing.
Nora (neutral): Nobody passes here, Max. The road ends at the farm.
Max (sad): Five minutes. That's all I'm asking.
Nora (neutral): No.
Max (angry): You can't just keep saying no.
Nora (neutral): Watch me.
@walk max 18.0 4.3 nowait
> He goes. He'll be back. She knows that walk.
@wait 2.0
Nora (worried): ...I should talk to Rebecca.
@journal note Max came back | He said he was passing. Nobody passes here. I think it's time I told Rebecca.
@set max_report_open
@camera player

== max_arrest
@trigger event max_arrest
@requires max_reported
@once
@fade out 0.8
@place nora 9.8 3.0 90
@place max 18.0 4.3 270
@place rebecca 25.0 4.4 270
@camera 12.4 3.2 9
@fade in 1.0
> The grey car is at the end of the lane again. He gets out as if he had never left.
@walk max 11.6 2.7
@face max nora
@face nora max
@camera between max nora 6
Max (warm): Nor. I've had time to think. Let's just talk.
Nora (neutral): I said no, Max.
@walk rebecca 10.8 4.7
@face max rebecca
@face rebecca max
@camera between max rebecca 7
Rebecca (neutral): She did. More than once.
Max (surprised): Who are you?
Rebecca (neutral): Officer Rebecca, Maple Grove. You were told to leave this farm, and you came back.
Max (angry): This is ridiculous. Nora. Tell her.
Nora (neutral): I already told you.
Rebecca (neutral): You're coming with me, sir. There's a court order to arrange, and after that a long drive home.
> For once he has nothing to say.
@walk max 25.0 4.4 nowait
@walk rebecca 24.0 4.0
> She walks him down the lane to her car. The grey one sits there until a tow truck comes for it.
@wait 1.5
Nora (warm): ...Okay.
@set max_arrested
@home rebecca off
@journal note Max is gone | Rebecca was waiting for him at the end of the lane. She took him away, and I didn't have to say another word. I don't think I'll see him again.
@camera player
